# The reference (PPDRIVER image): the pristine launcher boots Lemmings to its
# title menu, which reads LEVELDAT before any click, and on a click on
# "1 PLAYER" loads the first level's data (LEVELDAT
# is read earlier, at the title, in every run). Every read after `files-dir` is D15R's own, through BIOS
# Rwabs on drive C with 1,024-byte logical sectors; the record numbers are
# those of tools/dev/make_disks.sh's image. The menu is mouse-driven: the
# `mouse` step puts the game's cursor on "1 PLAYER" and `event doubleclick`
# clicks it. In Hatari the game then crashes in its level-preview code with an
# address error, so this ends at the level load.
expect start-tos Pexec\(0, "C:\\LEMMINGS\\START\.TOS"
expect pch Fopen\("LEMMINGS\.PCH"
expect ls2dd Fopen\("LS2DD\.FIC"
expect files-dir Dsetpath\("FILES"\)
expect root-dir Rwabs\(0,0x[0-9a-f]+,1,65,2\)
expect psyglogo Rwabs\(0,0x60000,8,387,2\)
expect dmalogo Rwabs\(0,0x68000,8,397,2\)
expect main-file Rwabs\(0,0xa00,100,815,2\)
expect intropar Rwabs\(0,0x10000,80,415,2\)
expect code-file Rwabs\(0,0xa00,76,499,2\)
expect leveldat Rwabs\(0,0x[0-9a-f]+,2,677,2\)
quiet title 4
shot title
mouse 70 150
sleep 0.5
event doubleclick
expect level-020 Rwabs\(0,0x41800,2,407,2\)
sleep 3
shot preview
